2. Attribution visible on screen

When this software, a modified version, or a product incorporating a
substantial part of it is presented to users on a screen, the normal
interface must visibly credit the original game and creator and provide
these references:

  Original game: Tupi Battle Grounds (TBG)
  Creator credit: Alexandre Zanata (@AlexandreZanata)
  Creator's GitHub: https://github.com/AlexandreZanata
  Original repository:
    https://github.com/AlexandreZanata/TBG-Tupi-Battle-Grounds

The credit must remain readable during normal use, including gameplay.
A footer or comparable persistent credit is acceptable. It must not be
removed, made illegible, covered, or confined to source code, documentation,
an optional credits screen or an acknowledgment shown only at first launch.
The creator and repository references must be clearly labeled clickable
links. If an interface cannot offer clickable links, display the full URLs
as readable text with the credit instead. You may translate or restyle the
credit while retaining the game's identity, the creator's identity and both
original destinations.

3. Copies and downstream use

Keep this license and its copyright notice with redistributed copies and
substantial portions of the covered material. You may choose additional
terms for your own contributions, but must preserve the permissions and
visible-attribution obligations for the material covered here. Passing a
copy to another party does not remove that party's attribution obligations.
Credit identifies the original author; it must not imply that the author
endorses your changes or business.

4. Third-party material

This license applies only to material for which the project owner can grant
